<%# locals: (sections:) %>
<%# A FILE PAGE'S COLUMN (Shop manual spec §7, slice 6): the page's own sections as in-page links,
    as Home's column carries its own, then the Library's column unchanged (layouts/column/_library:
    the folder tree, open down to this file's folder, then 3D models and Trash), whose lit row is this file's
    folder (design-system.md rule 8). `sections` is [label, id, note] for each section the page
    renders, decided by files/show.html.erb from the same conditions that render them, so a section
    that leaves the page cannot leave its link (shell_layout_test.rb holds every in-page link to an
    element the page carries). A section link lights nothing: it is a place on this page. %>
<div class="column-group">
  <h2 class="column-head">On this page</h2>
  <% sections.each do |label, id, note| %>
    <%= column_row label, "##{id}", note: note %>
  <% end %>
</div>
<%= render "layouts/column/library" %>
